# Goal 7: Fix __ctans / __ctansf — timeout (infinite loop)

## Functions
- __ctans, __ctansf

## Source Files
- C: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexd/ctand.c, /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexf/ctanf.c
- Rust: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s1/src/complexd.rs, /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s1/src/complexf.rs

## Problem
bridge_ctans and bridge_ctansf both TIMEOUT, meaning the Rust implementation enters an infinite loop or extremely long computation. This causes 4 test cases (2 per function) to be missing from the output.

Likely causes:
- A loop termination condition was incorrectly transpiled
- A convergence check uses the wrong comparison or threshold
- An iterative algorithm doesn't converge due to a sign or constant error

## What Needs to Change
1. Compare the Rust __ctans implementation against C source (ctand.c)
2. Compare the Rust __ctansf implementation against C source (ctanf.c)
3. Identify the loop or iterative section and fix the termination condition
4. Ensure the function returns in bounded time for all inputs

## Success Criteria
- bridge_ctans completes without timeout and produces correct output for all test inputs
- bridge_ctansf completes without timeout and produces correct output for all test inputs
- All 4 previously missing test cases now appear in the output with bitwise-exact matches
